      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "if I label this star"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 353.51,
      "end": 353.52,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "that if"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 353.52,
      "end": 356.83,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "minus c2 over c1"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 356.84,
      "end": 360.51,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "strictly larger than zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 366.31,
      "end": 366.32,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "t star exists."
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 366.32,
      "end": 367.83,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "So if"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 367.84,
      "end": 370.99,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "we have a solution, there is only one."
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 371.0,
      "end": 372.67,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "Which and this is regardless of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 372.68,
      "end": 373.87,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "initial condition that we would be"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 373.88,
      "end": 376.11,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "given. So the system cannot cross the"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 376.12,
      "end": 378.31,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "equilibrium position more than once."
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 378.32,
      "end": 380.83,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "So now let's look at what"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 380.84,
      "end": 382.43,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "we're doing here"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 382.44,
      "end": 386.39,
      "duration": 3.95,
      "text": "graphically."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 387.87,
      "end": 387.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So let's assume that we're for for"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 387.88,
      "end": 390.51,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "example starting with initial condition"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 390.52,
      "end": 392.67,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "here where we're stretching our our"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 392.68,
      "end": 395.23,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "spring, but we start with zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 395.24,
      "end": 397.71,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "velocity. So x dot of zero equals to"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 397.72,
      "end": 399.79,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "zero. That was the system that we had."
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 399.8,
      "end": 401.47,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "Then this is an over damped case where"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 401.48,
      "end": 403.59,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "both basically exponentials are decaying"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 403.6,
      "end": 406.39,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "to zero and so we would have"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 406.4,
      "end": 408.95,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "a solution that would go to zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 408.96,
      "end": 411.11,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "quickly. It would be damped."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 411.12,
      "end": 413.47,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "And so this would be"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 413.48,
      "end": 415.99,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "part part one. Now let's look at what"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 416.0,
      "end": 417.35,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "would happen if we start with other"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 417.36,
      "end": 419.27,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "initial conditions. So for example,"
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 419.28,
      "end": 422.47,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "starting with a velocity"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 422.48,
      "end": 424.35,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "starting from the same point"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 424.36,
      "end": 426.55,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "with a a much bigger velocity, then the"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 426.56,
      "end": 428.47,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "system would basically go up, but"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 428.48,
      "end": 432.19,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "eventually it has to go down."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 432.2,
      "end": 433.87,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "Well, it wouldn't it wouldn't have this"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 433.88,
      "end": 435.67,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "shape, but basically would have to go"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 435.68,
      "end": 438.71,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "down and not to to zero's position."
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 438.72,
      "end": 440.75,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "And when it reaches you can show that"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 440.76,
      "end": 444.07,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "again it can the derivative of x can"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 444.08,
      "end": 446.27,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "reach zero only"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 446.28,
      "end": 448.63,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "once and at that point you're then back"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 448.64,
      "end": 450.31,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "to the initial conditions that you had"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 450.32,
      "end": 452.07,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "in the first part of the question and so"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 452.08,
      "end": 453.87,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "you can then from here argue again that"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 453.88,
      "end": 456.43,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "you cannot cross the zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 456.44,
      "end": 458.71,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "the equilibrium point after after"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 458.72,
      "end": 460.27,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "reaching a maximum."
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 460.28,
      "end": 462.87,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "Now what if we had a stretch that would"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 462.88,
      "end": 465.87,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "be"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 468.39,
      "end": 468.4,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "and giving a negative velocity"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 468.4,
      "end": 471.63,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "to the to the mass and it very strong"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 471.64,
      "end": 473.55,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "negative velocity, then the system also"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 473.56,
      "end": 476.19,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "wants to go back to zero, but oh could"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 476.2,
      "end": 478.87,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "overshoot."
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 478.88,
      "end": 481.27,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "And the overshoot"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 481.28,
      "end": 484.15,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "would also generate a a unique time at"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 484.16,
      "end": 485.91,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "which the derivative would be equal to"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 485.92,
      "end": 487.55,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "zero and after that point you would be"
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 487.56,
      "end": 489.87,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "back to the same argument we had before"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 489.88,
      "end": 492.35,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "where the solution would have to"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 492.36,
      "end": 494.55,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "go towards zero, but never crosses it."
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 494.56,
      "end": 496.31,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "So we can have various configuration and"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 496.32,
      "end": 498.31,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "here I start with this point, but you"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 498.32,
      "end": 500.71,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "could also start"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 500.72,
      "end": 501.59,
      "duration": 0.87,
      "text": "with"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 501.6,
      "end": 503.63,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "other initial conditions where you could"
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 503.64,
      "end": 506.15,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "have as well something that would be for"
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 506.16,
      "end": 508.15,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "example um"
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 508.16,
      "end": 512.709,
      "duration": 4.549,
      "text": "very strong positive"
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 514.469,
      "end": 514.479,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "where again"
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 514.479,
      "end": 516.149,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "here you would have an overshoot, but"
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 516.159,
      "end": 517.51,
      "duration": 1.351,
      "text": "then the solution would be attracted"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 517.52,
      "end": 521.07,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "back by the x equal to zero solution."
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 521.08,
      "end": 522.19,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "Um"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 522.2,
      "end": 523.79,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "and of course you can also start from"
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 523.8,
      "end": 525.75,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "the equilibrium. If you're not imposing"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 525.76,
      "end": 527.43,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "an initial velocity we just stay there"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 527.44,
      "end": 529.07,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "because this is not forced, but if"
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 529.08,
      "end": 530.47,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "you're imposing a velocity, then you"
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 530.48,
      "end": 532.63,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "would have other trajectories"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 532.64,
      "end": 535.59,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "of the kind"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 535.6,
      "end": 538.47,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "for example um"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 538.48,
      "end": 541.35,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 543.55,
      "end": 543.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Where again it would"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 543.56,
      "end": 545.59,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "go up, but then be attracted back by the"
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 545.6,
      "end": 547.47,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "zero solution. So that's the typical"
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 547.48,
      "end": 549.43,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "behavior for a damped oscillator where"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 549.44,
      "end": 551.39,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "basically there's no oscillation, but"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 551.4,
      "end": 553.35,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "the solution is just attracted to to"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 553.36,
      "end": 555.23,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "rest and you could have cases of"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 555.24,
      "end": 558.43,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "overshoot, but it can show that"
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 558.44,
      "end": 561.07,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "that after the the overshoot the"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 561.08,
      "end": 563.19,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "velocity would reach zero with a maximum"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 563.2,
      "end": 565.03,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "and then would be attracted back to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 565.04,
      "end": 567.15,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "zero solution with never crossing it."
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 567.16,
      "end": 570.68,
      "duration": 3.52,
      "text": "And that ends this recitation."
    }
